"an empty list trusts nothing ... degrades the guards to their no-records fail-open behavior" — but reworkConsumption.parseMarkers treats empty allowlist as `null` = trust EVERYONE. Inconsistent! Let me re-check reworkConsumption.parseMarkers: `allow = (opts && Array.isArray(opts.authorLogins) && opts.authorLogins.length) ? opts.authorLogins : null` — empty → null → no filtering → trust everyone. Hmm, that contradicts the doctrine... but for restore_rework_arm, `unresolvedMachineThreadCount` returns 0 when no logins ("no identity, no trusted machine threads") → shouldRestoreArm gets unresolvedMachineThreads=0 → 'no-unresolved-threads' → no restore. So the restore sweep is inert without machine identity even though marker parsing trusts everyone. OK.

For my guard: if machineLogins is empty, `parseLapMarkers(comments, {authorLogins: []})` → trusts everyone → forged markers could withhold the arm. To follow the "empty list trusts nothing" doctrine properly in the guard: skip the guard when logins are empty (fail-open = arm as before). I'll add that check in both call sites: only consult guard when verdictMachineLogins(...).length > 0.

